   "pending": "'Tales to Tell' is Keeper's real Shield pool: gained with grantShield and read with ref:shield, so it still absorbs incoming damage like ordinary Shield. The engine exposes grantShield but NO shield-SPEND primitive, so each 'attempts to consume N Shield' (Page-turner, Character Development, Plot Armor, Hero's Return) is a guard `ref:shield >= N` followed by a custom `consumeShield` node -- the four customs. Modeling the pool as a plain `stack` would remove custom but lose the damage-absorbing property the oracle's word 'Shield' implies, so real Shield was chosen. The passive's essence-coupling fires on statusApplied; the engine has no event-status-kind condition, so it keys on eventUnit (an ally, not self) newly holding elemental_essence -- this over-fires only when an already-essenced ally receives some other status."
