   "name": "The Devil's Price",
   "description": "Whenever a target triggers one of Scratch's Deal skills, Scratch gains Elemental Essence. When one of his Deal skills expires without being triggered, its target gains Elemental Essence.",
   "pending": "Realized distributively across the Deal skills rather than as a single standalone trigger, because the engine offers no generic 'match any of these named marks' condition. (1) 'target triggers a Deal -> Scratch gains Essence' is the applyStatus{elemental_essence} to self inside each Deal's skillUsed reaction trigger below. (2) 'a Deal expires untriggered -> its target gains Essence' is the onExpire:[applyStatus{elemental_essence} to target] carried on each Deal-mark; onExpire fires only on a natural duration lapse, so a Deal that WAS triggered (its mark removed early by the reaction) never grants the target Essence. Each Deal is one mark applied to the target for the Deal window + a standing Scratch-owned reaction trigger gated on that mark. The ultimate 'Deal: Know Your Fate' has no 'use a skill' trigger and so does not participate in this economy (see its note)."
